{"id":"n5_u06_l1","unit_id":"n5_u06","instructional_level":"N5","title":"Family: mine and yours","goal":"Name family members, and learn the two sets of words (own and someone else's).","introduces":{"vocab":["v_kazoku","v_chichi","v_haha","v_ani","v_ane","v_otouto","v_imouto","v_otousan","v_okaasan","v_oniisan","v_oneesan","v_ryoushin"]},"explain":[{"heading":"Two sets of words","body":["Japanese uses different words for your own family and for someone else's. For your own family speaking to others: ちち, はは, あに, あね, おとうと, いもうと. For another person's family, add respect: おとうさん, おかあさん, おにいさん, おねえさん.","りょうしん means \"parents\" and かぞく means \"family\"."],"examples":[{"ja":"わたし の ちち は いしゃ です","reading":"watashi no chichi wa isha desu","en":"My father is a doctor."},{"ja":"おとうさん は かいしゃいん です か","reading":"otousan wa kaishain desu ka","en":"Is your father a company employee?"}]}],"practice":{"question_ids":["q_n5u06_mt01","q_n5u06_mt02","q_n5u06_fa01","q_n5u06_fa02","q_n5u06_fa03","q_n5u06_fa04","q_n5u06_fa05","q_n5u06_ty01","q_n5u06_ty02","q_n5u06_ty03","q_n5u06_dc01","q_n5u06_dc02","q_n5u06_dc03","q_n5u06_dc04","q_n5u06_gl01","q_n5u06_gl02","q_n5u06_gl03","q_n5u06_gl04","q_n5u06_vm_kazoku","q_n5u06_vm_chichi","q_n5u06_vm_haha","q_n5u06_vm_ani","q_n5u06_vm_ane","q_n5u06_vm_otouto","q_n5u06_vm_imouto","q_n5u06_vm_otousan","q_n5u06_vm_okaasan","q_n5u06_vm_oniisan","q_n5u06_vm_oneesan","q_n5u06_vm_ryoushin"]},"exit_check":{"question_ids":["q_n5u06_mt01","q_n5u06_mt02","q_n5u06_fa01","q_n5u06_fa02","q_n5u06_fa05","q_n5u06_ty01","q_n5u06_gl01","q_n5u06_gl03"],"pass":0.7},"provenance":"orig"},
{"id":"n5_u06_l2","unit_id":"n5_u06","instructional_level":"N5","title":"Jobs and things","goal":"Name common jobs and personal items.","introduces":{"vocab":["v_isha","v_daigakusei","v_enjinia","v_tenin","v_shufu","v_kangoshi","v_saifu","v_megane","v_tegami","v_tawaa","v_chiketto","v_omiyage"]},"explain":[{"heading":"Jobs and items","body":["いしゃ (doctor), だいがくせい (university student), エンジニア (engineer), てんいん (shop clerk), しゅふ (homemaker), かんごし (nurse). Items: さいふ (wallet), めがね (glasses), てがみ (letter).","タワー, チケット and おみやげ appear on a tower visit."],"examples":[{"ja":"あね は かんごし です","reading":"ane wa kangoshi desu","en":"My older sister is a nurse."},{"ja":"チケット は ここ です","reading":"chiketto wa koko desu","en":"Tickets are here."}]}],"practice":{"question_ids":["q_n5u06_ty04","q_n5u06_ty05","q_n5u06_ty06","q_n5u06_tr01","q_n5u06_tr02","q_n5u06_tr03","q_n5u06_tr04","q_n5u06_tr09","q_n5u06_so02","q_n5u06_vm_isha","q_n5u06_vm_daigakusei","q_n5u06_vm_enjinia","q_n5u06_vm_tenin","q_n5u06_vm_shufu","q_n5u06_vm_kangoshi","q_n5u06_vm_saifu","q_n5u06_vm_megane","q_n5u06_vm_tegami","q_n5u06_vm_tawaa","q_n5u06_vm_chiketto","q_n5u06_vm_omiyage"]},"exit_check":{"question_ids":["q_n5u06_ty04","q_n5u06_ty05","q_n5u06_ty06","q_n5u06_tr01","q_n5u06_tr04","q_n5u06_tr09"],"pass":0.7},"provenance":"orig"},
{"id":"n5_u06_l3","unit_id":"n5_u06","instructional_level":"N5","title":"の: A の B","goal":"Say whose thing it is: my wallet, my friend's letter.","introduces":{"vocab":["v_minna","v_watashitachi"],"grammar":["g_no_possessive"]},"explain":[{"heading":"Owner の thing","body":["の links two nouns. The owner goes first: わたし の さいふ (my wallet), ともだち の てがみ (my friend's letter).","You can drop the thing when it is clear: これ は わたし の です (\"this is mine\"). Ask だれ の です か (\"whose is it?\")."],"examples":[{"ja":"この かさ は だれ の です か","reading":"kono kasa wa dare no desu ka","en":"Whose is this umbrella?"},{"ja":"その かさ は わたし の です","reading":"sono kasa wa watashi no desu","en":"That umbrella is mine."}]}],"practice":{"question_ids":["q_n5u06_gn01","q_n5u06_gn02","q_n5u06_gn03","q_n5u06_gn04","q_n5u06_gn05","q_n5u06_tr05","q_n5u06_tr06","q_n5u06_so01","q_n5u06_vm_minna","q_n5u06_vm_watashitachi"]},"context":{"question_ids":["q_n5u06_gn06","q_n5u06_gn07"]},"exit_check":{"question_ids":["q_n5u06_gn01","q_n5u06_gn02","q_n5u06_gn04","q_n5u06_gn05","q_n5u06_gn07","q_n5u06_tr05"],"pass":0.7},"provenance":"orig"},
{"id":"n5_u06_l4","unit_id":"n5_u06","instructional_level":"N5","title":"も and じゃ ありません","goal":"Say \"also\" and \"is not\".","introduces":{"vocab":["v_sou","v_chigaimasu","v_hontou"],"grammar":["g_mo_also","g_ja_arimasen"]},"explain":[{"heading":"も: also","body":["も replaces は and adds \"too\": わたし も がくせい です. For \"both\": ちち も はは も いしゃ です."],"examples":[{"ja":"たなか さん も せんせい です","reading":"tanaka san mo sensei desu","en":"Ms. Tanaka is also a teacher."}]},{"heading":"じゃ ありません: is not","body":["The polite negative of です is じゃ ありません. わたし は いしゃ じゃ ありません. Answer a question with いいえ, then the negative. そう です means \"that is right\"; ちがいます means \"no, that is wrong\"."],"examples":[{"ja":"わたし は いしゃ じゃ ありません","reading":"watashi wa isha ja arimasen","en":"I am not a doctor."}]}],"practice":{"question_ids":["q_n5u06_gm01","q_n5u06_gm02","q_n5u06_gm03","q_n5u06_gm04","q_n5u06_gj01","q_n5u06_gj02","q_n5u06_gj03","q_n5u06_gj04","q_n5u06_gj05","q_n5u06_tr10","q_n5u06_vm_sou","q_n5u06_vm_chigaimasu","q_n5u06_vm_hontou"]},"context":{"question_ids":["q_n5u06_gm05","q_n5u06_gm06","q_n5u06_gj06"]},"exit_check":{"question_ids":["q_n5u06_gm01","q_n5u06_gm02","q_n5u06_gm04","q_n5u06_gj01","q_n5u06_gj02","q_n5u06_gj04","q_n5u06_gj05"],"pass":0.7},"provenance":"orig"},
{"id":"n5_u06_l5","unit_id":"n5_u06","instructional_level":"N5","title":"At the tower","goal":"Handle a short tower visit: tickets, the elevator, souvenirs.","introduces":{"vocab":["v_erebeetaa","v_otearai","v_chizu"]},"explain":[{"heading":"A tower visit","body":["Buy a チケット, take the エレベーター, look at the ちず (map), find the おてあらい and the おみやげ shop."],"examples":[{"ja":"エレベーター は あそこ です","reading":"erebeetaa wa asoko desu","en":"The elevator is over there."}]}],"practice":{"question_ids":["q_n5u06_dg01","q_n5u06_dg02","q_n5u06_dg03","q_n5u06_dg04","q_n5u06_dg05","q_n5u06_dg08","q_n5u06_so03","q_n5u06_ty07","q_n5u06_vm_erebeetaa","q_n5u06_vm_otearai","q_n5u06_vm_chizu"]},"context":{"question_ids":["q_n5u06_dg06","q_n5u06_dg07"]},"exit_check":{"question_ids":["q_n5u06_dg01","q_n5u06_dg03","q_n5u06_dg05","q_n5u06_dg08","q_n5u06_so03","q_n5u06_ty07"],"pass":0.7},"provenance":"orig"},
{"id":"n5_u06_l6","unit_id":"n5_u06","instructional_level":"N5","title":"Kanji: 人 大 小 山 川 上 下 中","goal":"Learn eight common kanji.","introduces":{"kanji":["k_hito","k_dai","k_shou","k_yama","k_kawa","k_ue","k_shita","k_naka"],"vocab":["v_shita","v_naka"]},"explain":[{"heading":"Eight everyday kanji","body":["人 is a person (ひと), 大 is big, 小 is small, 山 is a mountain (やま), 川 is a river (かわ), 上 is above (うえ), 下 is below (した), 中 is the middle or inside (なか).","Kanji can have several readings. Here they are shown with furigana until you have learned them."],"examples":[{"ja":"山 と 川","reading":"yama to kawa","en":"mountains and rivers"},{"ja":"山 の 上","reading":"yama no ue","en":"the top of a mountain"}]}],"practice":{"question_ids":["q_n5u06_tr07","q_n5u06_tr08","q_n5u06_ty08","q_n5u06_kd01","q_n5u06_kd02","q_n5u06_kd03","q_n5u06_kd04","q_n5u06_kd05","q_n5u06_kd06","q_n5u06_kd07","q_n5u06_kd08","q_n5u06_kk01","q_n5u06_kk02","q_n5u06_kk03","q_n5u06_kk04","q_n5u06_kk05","q_n5u06_kk06","q_n5u06_kmt01","q_n5u06_kmt02","q_n5u06_kcf01","q_n5u06_kcf02","q_n5u06_kcf03","q_n5u06_vm_shita","q_n5u06_vm_naka"]},"exit_check":{"question_ids":["q_n5u06_kd01","q_n5u06_kd02","q_n5u06_kd04","q_n5u06_kd06","q_n5u06_kk01","q_n5u06_kk03","q_n5u06_kmt01","q_n5u06_kcf02"],"pass":0.7},"provenance":"orig"},
{"id":"n5_u06_l7","unit_id":"n5_u06","instructional_level":"N5","title":"Listen and read","goal":"Follow family words and signs.","introduces":{},"explain":[{"heading":"Longer sounds","body":["Family words are often heard with long vowels: おにいさん, おねえさん. Listen for the extra beat."],"examples":[{"ja":"おにいさん","reading":"oniisan","en":"(someone's) older brother"}]}],"practice":{"question_ids":["q_n5u06_gl05","q_n5u06_gl06","q_n5u06_gl07","q_n5u06_gl08"]},"context":{"question_ids":["q_n5u06_rq01","q_n5u06_rq02","q_n5u06_rq03","q_n5u06_rq04","q_n5u06_rq05"]},"exit_check":{"question_ids":["q_n5u06_gl05","q_n5u06_gl06","q_n5u06_gl07","q_n5u06_rq01","q_n5u06_rq04"],"pass":0.7},"provenance":"orig"},
